   198	cases=1006 mismatches=0
   199	```
   200	
   201	Finite evidence supports the float-contract adequacy bridge; it is not used as
   202	a universal proof.
   203	
   204	## Excluded behavior
   205	
   206	- Lists shorter than two and lists containing non-`Float` values.
   207	- Exceptions and out-of-bounds behavior outside the stated precondition.
   208	- A formal total-correctness/termination theorem.
   209	- A K-internal theorem that the fold result minimizes mathematical distance
   210	  independently of the supplied opaque float contracts.
   211	- A Python/K adequacy claim for NaN or other special IEEE edge behavior.

